WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.840 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
Nothing in your business happens without
you, and it's starting to wear you down,

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:07.580 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
You're on your phone at all hours
answering the same questions, making the

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:12.320 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
same decisions, putting out the same fires
long after everyone else has clocked off.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.800 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
And you tell yourself this
is just what it takes.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.080 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
Every founder goes through it, but
that's the story that keeps you stuck.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.980 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
This isn't what running a business looks
like, it's what a business looks like when

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.710 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
everything still runs through you.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:27.280 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
I'm Nuno, and I help founders bring
structure to the chaos so the business can

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:29.990 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
run without them holding
every piece of it together.

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:32.200 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
Picture this, your team
makes the day-to-day

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:35.260 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
calls, without coming to
you. The same problem gets

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:38.080 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
solved the same way every
time, whether you're in

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:40.540 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
the room or not, and you
finally get to step back

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.170 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
from the firefighting and
think about where this

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:44.530 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
business is
actually going.

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:47.440 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
Let me tell you where most of the
founders are when they come to me.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:50.050 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
You've got a strategy in
your head, things you want

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:52.680 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
to build, where you want
to be in five years, but

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:55.300 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
you never get to any of
it because every day gets

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:58.000 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
swallowed by the
day-to-day. Approvals,

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.310 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
questions, decisions your
team should be making

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:02.200 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
without you. Then you get
to the end of the day and

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:04.950 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
ask yourself what did I
actually move forward?

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:07.200 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
And the answer is almost nothing.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.480 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
You were busy every minute, but
you were reacting, not building.

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:12.810 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
If that's you right now,
that is the hard truth.

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:16.960 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
You don't own a business, you own a
job, one that depends entirely on you.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:20.700 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
And the moment you try to grow it breaks
because you can't be in every room at

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:24.080 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
once. The solution? The Vessel
Operating System method.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:28.140 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
So how do we fix it? A
bit of background first.

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:32.240 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
I spent six years as an officer in the
Portuguese Marines, then seven and a half

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:36.160 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
years at Amazon building operations
where things simply had to work.

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:39.800 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
Out of all that, I built my own
method of getting business in order.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:42.180 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
I call it the Vessel
Operating System, and it

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:44.320 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
has three parts.
First, the Bridge.

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:46.840 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
That's your strategy,
where the business really

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:49.210 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
is and where you
actually want to take it.

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:51.450 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
Before anything else,
we get clear on the

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:55.410 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
destination. Second, the
Hull. That's what keeps

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:58.570 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
you afloat. Your systems,
your processes, your cash.

00:01:58.570 --> 00:02:01.190 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
This is where we build the
structure your team can

00:02:01.190 --> 00:02:03.520 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
follow so decisions
stop coming back to you.

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:07.560 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
Third, the Cargo Hold.
That's what the business

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:11.110 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
carries. Your product and
how you take it to market.

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:14.260 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
I score every part of it,
so we see where the real

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:16.560 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
gaps are, not where
you think they are.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:19.340 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
Because often what you
believe is the problem

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:22.880 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
isn't the problem at all.
Then we get to work in

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:25.300 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
focused 90-day plans: a
handful of projects at a

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:28.120 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
time, all measured, so
you can see it working.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:30.470 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
And I don't hand you a plan and walk away.

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:35.520 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
You and your team do the building, and I'm
with you every step because implementation

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:37.550 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
is the part that actually changes things.

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:40.080 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
Let me show you what this
looks like in practice.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:42.220 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
With the production
agency, we got the whole

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:44.750 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
team aligned on where the
business was going and

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:47.740 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
made the organisation
leaner and more efficient

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:50.830 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
along the way. With that
same agency, we improved

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:52.910 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
their communication
systems and cut the time

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:55.520 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
the founder spends making
decisions by around 20%.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:58.970 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
And with a clinical
psychology practice, we

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:02.100 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
defined a new service and
worked out exactly who it

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.280 line:83% position:75% size:46% align:center
was for and how
to reach them.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:06.800 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
Now picture where this gets you.

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:08.480 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
Not just in the business, but at home.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:12.240 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
The founders I work with tell me
that's where they notice it the most.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:15.280 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
They sleep better, they are off their
phones in the evening, they've got time

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:18.400 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
for their family again and for
the things they used to enjoy.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:21.270 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
Because there's no real
line between work and home.

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:25.560 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
If the business is a mess, you don't get
to walk through the door and switch it

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:27.540 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
off, fix one and fix the other.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:31.440 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
So if that's where you want to
get to, here's the first step.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.890 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
Hit the button below
and book a call with me.

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:38.580 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
It's 30 minutes. It's a real conversation
about where you are at and whether we are

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:42.410 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
the right fit for each other. You'll
get a straight answer either way.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:46.620 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
This is hands-on work, so I only take
on a small number of founders at a time.

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:48.170 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
That's how the quality stays high.

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:52.390 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
So if you are ready to stop running a job
and start owning a business, book your

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:56.250 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
call below. Thanks for watching.

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:57.880 line:83% position:50% size:86% align:center
Speak soon.
